  "sdo:name": "Com-Vida CAIC Project",
  "sdo:description": "The Com-Vida CAIC Project promotes environmental awareness and ocean literacy among children and adolescents at the Ayrton Senna da Silva Integrated Center for Child and Adolescent Support in Balneário Camboriú, Brazil. Grounded in UNESCO’s Education for Sustainable Development framework, the project engages students as active agents in building a sustainable future through collective actions such as waste reduction, recycling campaigns, and monitoring the river-to-ocean pathway. By integrating science, citizenship, and creativity, Com-Vida CAIC fosters ecological thinking and community engagement, connecting local initiatives to the global goals of the United Nations Decade of Ocean Science for Sustainable Development (2021–2030).",
